course: dictionary
lesson: 14925
title: Refuge, a safe place
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Refuge means safety from danger, trouble or bad weather. You can also use it for a place that gives that safety. «After the storm, the hikers took refuge in a small mountain hut.» The hut was a place where they were safe from the storm.
explain: Refuge is often used in phrases such as «take refuge», «seek refuge» and «a place of refuge». When someone seeks refuge, they are looking for a safe place to escape danger. «The family had to leave their home and seek refuge in another country.» Here the family wanted safety from danger.
explain: You will also meet refuge on busy roads and in nature. «Stand on the refuge in the middle of the road until the cars have passed.» A refuge on a road is a small safe island where you can stop while crossing. «The wildlife refuge gives hurt birds a safe place to get better.» It protects animals.
fact: Refuge means safety or shelter from danger, trouble or bad weather.
fact: A refuge can also be a place that gives that safety, such as a mountain hut, a wildlife refuge or a safe house.
fact: «Seek refuge» and «take refuge» both mean going to a safe place to get away from danger.
fact: A traffic island in the middle of a busy road is a refuge, because it keeps people safe while they cross.
fact: A person who is given refuge in another country may be called a refugee.
exercise: «After the storm, the hikers took refuge in a small mountain hut.» What does refuge mean here? | A big hotel with a swimming pool | A map of the hills | A type of walking boot | *Shelter from the storm
exercise: «The wildlife refuge gives hurt birds a safe place to get better.» What is a wildlife refuge? | A race track for cyclists | *A safe place that protects animals | A school for birds | A shop that sells pet food
exercise: What do people do when they seek refuge? | Count their money | Start a race | *Go to a safe place to escape danger | Cook a big meal
test: Stand on the refuge in the middle of the busy road until the cars have passed. What is the refuge? | A kind of bicycle | A big puddle | *A safe island to stop on while crossing | A place to dance
test: «She found refuge from the noise in her quiet room.» What does refuge mean here? | A school trip | A loud noise | A bright light | *Safety and shelter from trouble
exam: Which sentence uses refuge correctly to mean a safe place? | *The lost lambs found refuge in the old barn from the snow | The lost lambs ate refuge for lunch | Refuge is my favourite colour | The refuge sang loudly on the hill
